Problem Description:
Find the bug and fix this 8-bit wide 2-to-1 mux.

// module top_module (
//     input sel,
//     input [7:0] a,
//     input [7:0] b,
//     output out  );

//     assign out = (~sel & a) | (sel & b);

// endmodule

module top_module (
	input sel,
	input [7:0] a,
	input [7:0] b,
	output reg [7:0] out
);

Erroneous Implementation:

always @(posedge clk or posedge reset) begin
	if (reset) begin
		out <= 8'b0;
	end else begin
		if (sel == 0) begin
			out <= b;
		end else begin
			out <= a;
		end
	end
end

endmodule

Feedback:
bugs_mux2.sv:164: error: Unable to bind wire/reg/memory `reset' in `tb.top_module1'
bugs_mux2.sv:164: error: Unable to elaborate condition expression.
2 error(s) during elaboration.

```verilog
module top_module (
    input sel,
    input [7:0] a,
    input [7:0] b,
    output [7:0] out
);

    // A 2-to-1 mux is a combinational circuit.
    // If sel is 0, out should be a.
    // If sel is 1, out should be b.
    assign out = sel ? b : a;

endmodule
```
